        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ea4c37f3-0899-5b38-b1ea-ba9c0c1a72d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: ESZ, Schott Music\n- People: Paul Hindemith, Igor Stravinsky, Carl Orff, Richard Strauss, Luigi Nono, Krzysztof Penderecki, Joaquín Rodrigo\n- Roles: Italian agent, composer, violist, violinist, teacher, conductor\n- Works: Das Marienleben, Der Schwanendreher, Mathis der Maler\n\nFacts:\n- Since the 1950s, ESZ has been the Italian agent of Schott Music.\n- Since the 1950s, ESZ has represented Schott Music composers including Igor Stravinsky, Carl Orff, Paul Hindemith, Richard Strauss, Luigi Nono, Krzysztof Penderecki, and Joaquín Rodrigo.\n- Paul Hindemith was born on 16 November 1895 and died on 28 December 1963.\n- Paul Hindemith was a prolific German composer, violist, violinist, teacher, and conductor.\n- Paul Hindemith composed the song cycle Das Marienleben in 1923.\n- Paul Hindemith composed Der Schwanendreher for viola and orchestra in 1935.\n- Paul Hindemith composed the opera Mathis der Maler in 1938.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
